A '''droid parts and repair shop'''<ref name="Andor 3" /> was located on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]],<ref name="Andor 1" /> at [[North Stairs Lane]],<ref name="Andor 3" /> across the street from [[Greyble Service]],<ref name="Andor 1" /> and near [[Gyo (business)|Gyo]].<ref name="Andor 3" /> [[Aurebesh]] lettering over the entrance read "DROID PARTS", although the O in "[[droid]]s" was upside-down. The sign was held up by a couple of unidentical [[protocol droid]] [[Limb|arms]].<ref name="Andor 1" /> Another sign for the business consisted of [[Color|red]] and yellow writing on a dark blue background. The top and bottom of the sign were written in Aurebesh and read "DROID PARTS" and "REPAIR SERVICE" respectively; while the middle was written in Bazeese and seemed to read "DROID PARTS", like the top of the sign.<ref name="Andor 3" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I originally drew it with astromech legs but we couldn't find any spare. But protocol droid arms were weirdly abundant & look better. There is also another droid shop sign painted on the top of that shop in a new font.|Graphic designer Barry Gingell on Twitter|<ref name="Twitter arms" />}}
The store was created for "[[Kassa (episode)|Kassa]]," the premiere episode of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''.<ref name="Andor 1" /> The sign was designed by graphic designers [[Elle McKee]] and [[Barry Gingell]]. Gingell originally drew the sign with [[astromech droid]] [[Limb|legs]], but when the sign was made, the production crew couldn't find any spare ones, so they went with [[protocol droid]] [[Limb|arms]] instead.<ref name="Twitter arms">{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1574871034842456074|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-09-22|quote=That was indeed a collaboration between myself & @MckeeElle. I originally drew it with astromech legs but we couldn't find any spare. But protocol droid arms were weirdly abundant & look better. There is also another droid shop sign painted on the top of that shop in a new font.|archivedate=20220928131023}}</ref> The graphic designer stated on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] that another sign was painted at the top of the shop<ref name="Twitter arms" /> in a new alphabet created for the series,<ref name="Twitter arms" /> but he was not in a position to reveals its name. It was the same script that appeared at the bottom of the [[Gavalox Communications]] sign<ref name="Twitter script">{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1574883352242429952|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-09-22|quote=You are correct. It is the same new script. It does have a name. I'm just not sure I have permission to reveal it haha. That's a @pabl0hidalgo or @PhilSzostak level thing. Above my paygrade.|archivedate=20220928135536}}</ref> in the episode "[[That Would Be Me]]"<ref name="Andor 2">{{Andor|That Would Be Me}}</ref> and on a sign on [[Greyble Service]] across the street.<ref name="Andor 1" /><ref name="Twitter script" /> The name of the alphabet was eventually revealed to be [[Bazeese script]], in the episode guide for "[[Rix Road (episode)|Rix Road]]."<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e12-trivia-gallery|text="Rix Road" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slides 2 and 5}}</ref>

The other sign mentioned by the graphic designer is barely seen on-screen; according to a vague Twitter post by Gingell, "You can briefly see the left of the sign behind the big alien guys <small>''[sic]''</small> head as they look up the street. Just a bit of red lettering." Since the post was made on [[September 27]], [[2022]],<ref name="Twitter elusive">{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1574878091142373400|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-09-27|quote=You can briefly see the left of the sign behind the big alien guys <small>''[sic]''</small> head as they look up the street. Just a bit of red lettering.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/RL9wg}}</ref> after the first three episodes of the series were released on [[Disney+]] on [[September 21]], but before the [[Aldhani (episode)|fourth episode]] was released on [[September 28]],<ref name="Release dates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-08-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref> and the business does not appear in the [[That Would Be Me|second episode]],<ref name="Me">{{Andor|That Would Be Me}}</ref> the scene in question must take place in either "Kassa"<ref name="Andor 1" /> or "[[Reckoning (episode)|Reckoning]]."<ref name="Andor 3" />

